<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yalangtush Bahadur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1576">1576</a>–<a href="/years/1656">1656</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Yalangtush Bi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yalangtush Bahadur was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> emir of the Alchin tribe who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> for the Ashtarkhanid khans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> in the first half of the seventeenth century. A leading military commander of the khanate, he is said to have helped the Kazakh khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahangir">Jahangir</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungars</a> in 1643. He built the Sher-Dor and Tilya-Kori <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasas</a>, which with the older <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulugh-beg">Ulugh Beg</a> madrasa frame the Registan in Samarkand.</p></div>
